    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "No it won't work neither because it mutates the internal helper's state. We don't have to call methods on the helper directly. What we have to do instead is (what is done inside [`connectMenu`](https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch.js/blob/develop/src/connectors/menu/connectMenu.js#L182-L183)) call the method on the `state` attribute. It won't mutate the internal helper state and return a fresh state.",
    "commit_id": "27b5a589fecd444a57205dd1ef3432c996be4e6a",
    "created_at": "2018-12-18T16:31:07Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -167,10 +170,16 @@ Learn more: https://community.algolia.com/instantsearch.js/v2/widgets/configure.\n             ? helper.setQueryParameter('hitsPerPage', undefined).search()\n             : helper.setQueryParameter('hitsPerPage', value).search();\n \n+        createURLFn = value => {\n+          this.setHitsPerPage(value);",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/algolia/instantsearch/pull/3363#discussion_r242609600",
